    "result_text": "All three findings addressed, and the build is green.\n\n## Changes made\n\nI agreed with all three findings:\n\n1. **Deleted the orphaned `Owner.region(String city, String postcode)`** (`model/Owner.java`). Confirmed via repo-wide search that its only production caller was the old `getLocality()`, which now uses `identityRegion(...)`/the customerCode prefix. The `OwnerPostcodes`/`ValidateOwnerPostcode` path uses `regionForCity`, so the method was dead.\n\n2. **Reconciled the \"single source of truth\" claims.** With `region()` gone, the contradiction disappears: `identityRegion` is the source of truth for the identity's region, `regionForCity` for the city mapping, `regionForPostcode` for the postcode mapping. I also fixed the two dangling `{@link #region(String, String)}` javadoc references (in `regionForCity` and `regionForPostcode`) \u2014 one pointed at `identityRegion`, the other dropped the stale reference.\n\n3. **Dropped the no-op `.toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)`** in `sha256UpperHex8` (`AssignCustomerCode.java`) since the `%02X` format already yields upper-case hex, and removed the now-unused `Locale` import.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` still passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
