        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe hash and identity-building logic is placed well (the `sha256UpperHex8` helper is local to `AssignCustomerCode`, and `identityRegion` sits on `Owner` as a shared source of truth reused by both `AssignCustomerCode` and `getLocality`). But the change introduces a second, overlapping region method without retiring the one it displaces, leaving duplicated/dead structure:\n\n1. **`Owner.region(String city, String postcode)` is now orphaned (`Owner.java:299`).** Its only production caller was the old `getLocality()`, which this diff rewrote to use `identityRegion(...)`/the customerCode prefix instead. A repo-wide search finds no remaining production caller (the `region(...)` references left are its own definition and javadoc; `OwnerPostcodes`/`ValidateOwnerPostcode` use `regionForCity`, and the test `AcceptanceBase.region(city)` is an unrelated method). It should be deleted so the model doesn't carry a dead public method.\n\n2. **Two methods both claim to be \"the single source of truth for region derivation.\"** `region(...)` javadoc (`Owner.java:290-298`) still says so, while the new `identityRegion` javadoc (`Owner.java:278-283`) says it is the single source of truth for the identity's region. With `region()` gone this contradiction disappears; if for some reason `region()` is kept, the two overlapping postcode-first-then-city vs postcode-only derivations and their competing \"source of truth\" claims need reconciling, because a maintainer can no longer tell which to call.\n\n3. **Minor redundancy in `sha256UpperHex8` (`AssignCustomerCode.java`).** The loop already formats bytes with `%02X` (upper-case hex), so the trailing `.toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)` on the assembled string is a no-op. Drop it (and the `Locale` import if it becomes unused) \u2014 the method name already promises upper-case.\n\nEverything else is coherent and idiomatic: the `EnsureCityCapacity` javadoc correctly drops its now-false \"as `AssignCustomerCode` does\" cross-reference, and the OpenAPI/`membershipNumber` doc updates track the new identity."
      }
